<title>FRANCE: CGIP seeks &quot;more generous&quot; Valeo payouts.</title>
<headline>CGIP seeks &quot;more generous&quot; Valeo payouts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>French holding company CGIP will seek a &quot;more generous&quot; payout policy from car parts maker Valeo, CGIP Chairman Ernest-Antoine Seilliere told a news conference on Monday.</p>
<p>CGIP is buying 20 percent of Valeo in a deal announced earlier on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;We will ask for a payout of a third of the net,&quot; Seilliere told reporters.</p>
<p>Valeo currently pays out about 15 to 18 percent of its net profit, while the average on the Paris stock exchange is 35 to 40 percent.</p>
<p>Earlier statements from CGIP and the other firms involved in the Valeo stake acquisitions said Valeo would make an advance dividend downpayment later this month of 10 francs per share.</p>
</text>
